{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/136655-hunter-homebrew-conspiracy-compact-expansion-night-job-merit","id":136655,"title":"Hunter Homebrew - Conspiracy/Compact Expansion - Night Job merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-14T07:30:14-07:00","id":136655,"title":"Hunter Homebrew - Conspiracy/Compact Expansion - Night Job merit","content":"My first post here and my first attempt at home-brew, inspired by the recent release of mortal remains<br /> Any constructive criticisms or contributions are more than welcome <b>Night Job</b><br /> <br /> I thought the idea of conspiracies and how they relate to Hunters day to day lives needed more fleshing out.<br /> Be warned I've been watching a lot of The Good Wife lately so I put a lot of lawyer characters and interaction in here<br /> but it also gives you options in ways to keep your Hunters out of the cross-hairs of the Local PD<br /> <br /> <b>Night Job</b> (merit dots limited by compact/conspiracy status)<br /> <br /> Your a full-time Hunter now, you have a job at one of your organisation's fronts, actually paying you to maintain the Vigil.<br /> Maybe you work as a concierge for the local Abbey clubhouse or as an agent at the local Vanguard field office,<br /> even \u201cworking\u201d as a paid intern at the University\u2019s history department (naturally run by the Aegis) keeps you in the hunt enough<br /> that you don't really worry about having to keep up appearances of being an upstanding citizen. High dots in this merit often mean<br /> high-paying and influential jobs within the organisation, such as a corporate executive or actually being a paid mercenary In the case<br /> of some of TF:V's Fronts<br /> <br /> Night jobs make a lot of sense for conspiracy members but not for most compacts. Not a lot of union members are down with supporting<br /> another hunter with a no-show job.Conspiracies however have built up power and infrastructure for just such arrangements.<br /> <br /> Some conspiracies have this as the norm of their operations, Vanguard and Cheiron in particular, how this merit is handled in these cases is up to ST.<br /> Dots of status in those organisations without dots of Night Job usually represent the fact that your still handling a lot of paperwork and grunt-work<br /> within the organisation and don't have as much time and company resources to dedicate to the Vigil so do not (yet) benefit from the merit.<br /> <br /> This merit allows characters to maintain an equivalent level of resources without the need to support it with an appropriate day job<br /> and provides cover for her hunting activities, any investigations into the characters life to find any irregularities<br /> takes a penalty equal to the merit dots, however investigations into actual crimes or actions done by the character<br /> take no penalty, this means that a murder scene investigation for a killing committed by the character won't be protected by this merit<br /> but her alibi would. Also each dot of Night job can be used to call an equivalent number of dots of ally from that job for each story<br /> <br /> Note that dots in night job do not automatically grant dot's in resources just provide a convenient means to gain them<br /> Discount cost on the resources merit is per ST removal, encouraged in the case of inventive or entertaining Night Job concepts<br /> <br /> Urlich has a four dot Night Job with the ascending ones, he works as a lieutenant for the boss of the west side distribution of drugs in Chicago.<br /> Urlich is able to maintain his four-dots of resources from his cut of the operation without actually doing much. Urlich's become a scarred up mean bastard since<br /> he started his Vigil and he gets high on stuff the other lieutenants can't even identify, so they all make sure everythings taken care of and trust whatever he contributes<br /> is worth his presence. The boss says stay away from him unless he asks for something, than up shut and do it, so they do.<br /> <br /> During our Urlich's adventures he identifies a troublesome ghoul running interference for his master, who remains out of their reach, particularly<br /> as his latest escapades have drawn the scrutiny of the local police. Urlich asks the ST if his Night Job would give him contact with a hit-man<br /> who could take care of the ghoul for him. It is decided that a hit-man is probably someone Urlich could acquire through his organisation, this is decided<br /> to be a three-dot ally, Timmy \u201cBones\u201d McCoy, a killer as reliable as he is conspicuous, leaving only one available dot of ally from night job<br /> for the rest of the story. When Urlich is inevitably brought in for questioning by the local police later on an unrelated matter he is only able to draw<br /> on one-dot ally from his his night job. In a previous story he was able to acquire hot-shot lawyer Deborah Sweet-man (four dots using all his night job points).<br /> This time it's her junior partner Don Wright for one point (Debbie\u2019s got the flu and she's on a cruise in the Caribbean, if it's any consolation she's miserable).<br /> Urlich makes bail but is still under investigation, Last time Deborah got them to drop the charges, destroy the evidence and apologise rather than risk a harassment suit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3016-prince-of-ashes","name":"Prince of Ashes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T07:41:00-07:00","id":136696,"title":"","content":"<b>Example Night Jobs and Fronts</b><br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge</b><br /> <br /> <b>Foxhound and Carver</b><br /> <br /> This international law firm has offices in every major city and maintains a legion of lawyers, para-legals, private investigators and \u201cresearchers\u201d (who do in fact have one of any number of jobs related to the archiving and research into the occult, particularly the Lucifuge's extensive genealogical records).<br /> Their head office in Milan, the \u201cBlack tower\u201d, dominates the city's skyline and goes even deeper underground, to vaults, archives and catacombs that predate even the inquisition.<br /> The group is old, really old, old old, almost Lucifuge old, the kind of old that doesn't leave a smell, it's just part of the fabric of reality and can be traced back through Milanese trade companies to pre-banking Merchant families.<br /> A lot of it's wealth is almost inexplicable to modern business eyes, and holds it's value to deals made with growing old money families that still hold sway today, contracts that follow through bloodlines. Families that make sure that their progeny know that the any price they have to pay pales in comparison to what they would suffer if they failed to honour the debt.<br /> F&amp;C in return ensures the success of those families, most of which also feature in the genealogical records the Lucifuge maintains. They don't get to ask for these favours, they are just made aware of them and can expect to be told what they need to do in return later. Don't feel guilty, when these old-money inbreds donate to the firm they're probably doing the only substantive thing they've ever done. It's all for a good cause right?<br /> Oh and if you rescue anyone rich, let your local firm contact know who to bill, don't worry, they'll pay, no one fucks with the Collections department.<br /> F&amp;C brings legal protection, investigative services, influence and most importantly money to the table. Just like any instrument of the Lucifuge they expect results, though care very little how you get them, your given a lot of autonomy but only expect support when the firm or the lucifuge decides it's in their interests.<br /> <br /> <b>Faustchild trust</b><br /> When people ask how a Law firm can have so much wealth and influence as F&amp;C, particularly in the business world (they seem to own a small slice of any major company older than the second world war).<br /> You get two words: Trust management. The firm is widely believed to represent and manage the trusts for dozens of influential families, that simply isn't true. They manage one trust for one family, the Lucifuge.<br /> Many promising family members are given new identities that put them down as beneficiaries for the world's largest trust fund, one that funds dozens of wayward young (and seemingly young) men and women<br /> all with reputations as debauched mindless fools who waste their inheritances on any vice they can get their hands on, what they really do in their spare time (which is all of their time) is far more salacious<br /> <br /> F&amp;C tapped you for the firm while you were still in Harvard Law, your parents were very.... Enthusiastic you take up their offer.<br /> Strangely you saw a little fear in your old man's eyes when you told him about it, something you'd never seen in the old tycoons steely eyes before.<br /> A few years in with the firm and you now know why, half the time you don't know what your doing or why and the rest of the time you wish you didn't but you do your best and follow orders.<br /> The pay doesn't hurt, not like you ever needed money, but the power? That was something else.<br /> Playing man behind the throne for half a dozen of New York's most influential families is a real buzz and the feeling you got when you started giving dear old dad orders made doing a line of coke of a Jasmine's chest seem positively mundane.<br /> Now you've got that promotion, heading up the new Montreal office.<br /> Problem is it's just you and two para-legals who almost wet themselves whenever you look at them.<br /> You just got to town and your first directive is to provide \u201cclose support\u201d for one of those Faustchild trustees and his friends. They have... unique problems that your expected to help with and damned if they won't just take your advice and stay out of trouble.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Jason Faustchild claims to be Lord Byron's descendant and it's easy to believe. With ethereal good looks, bad boy charm and penchant for making TMZ's Homepage with his latest antics make him a handful.<br /> Which is why his F&amp;C appointed attorney Elea McCray has spent the last two years cleaning up after him.<br /> During that time it was hard not falling under his spell.<br /> Elea's done a lot for him, visiting him in that private clinic he bought just so he wouldn't have to spend time in the hospital (The food is admittedly a lot better) either recovering from another overdose or ridiculous extreme sports accident (the exact nature of his injuries and problems always need to be hushed up).<br /> Than arranging alibi's for what he swears are just elaborate pranks.<br /> Providing cover during that month a team of Dominican mercenaries were out for his blood (he promises it was just a misunderstanding,but she never did find out how he sorted that out).<br /> But he's always looked out for her too, remembered her birthday, always a kind word, sent glowing reviews to her bosses.<br /> There was even that time he personally intervened when that stalker wouldn't leave her alone (For some reason he said it was his fault anyway).<br /> Jason seems to clean up his act around her, like he isn't really that guy, he seems older, wiser and a little weary.<br /> Not the manic-depressive party boy he presents to the world.<br /> When you meet someone special all those little flaws just become cute and you can't fight how you feel and Elea fell for him.<br /> These days it all makes a little more sense to Elea, now that she knows he's some sort of Occult Batman protecting the city from what goes bump in the night. Jason still keeps secrets, his identity is really just another cover story and now Elea wonders why he's always so coy about his age or why she has to keep fabricating any personal documents more than five years old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3016-prince-of-ashes","user":"Prince of Ashes","date":". 05-14-2014, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3016-prince-of-ashes","name":"Prince of Ashes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:04:02-07:00","id":138637,"title":"","content":"Can we argue that TFV agents are either Federal agents assigned to a specific &quot;task force&quot;, or are made part of a Delta Force-esque operation if they're actually on the Federal payroll already? And the civilians are part of front companies or &quot;paid consultancies&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T00:14:06-07:00","id":139069,"title":"","content":"I would say that there are a lot of possible occupations and covers for TFV agents<br /> There was even a team of TFV agents who were all local cops in some of the early Hunter material, they just received support and intel from TFV command<br /> <br /> The idea I have here is that the conspiracies are just that, conspiracies, multi-layered and self supporting but they all have some sort of central authority pulling the strings<br /> <br /> I imagine TFV supporting individual hunters and teams as deniable assets, supplying arms, intel and giving directives as needed with little direct involvement.<br /> Whilst also maintaining hunters attached to front organizations which could be private security or military companies and clandestine military/law enforcement divisions<br /> <br /> You could easily have delta operators recruited directly from the military into the &quot;Tactical Intelligence Interpretation Division&quot; that goes out on beyond black operations against foreign supernatural threats.<br /> Or the Department of Infrastructure Security which maintains a vague remit to protect America's public works and infrastructure from criminals and terrorists but actually operates entirely as a front to supply and pay agents to hunt monsters on American soil.<br /> <br /> I feel all of these options are valid and depend on what kind of game you want to run, they're even opportunities for intra-conspiracy rivalry, with Local deniable hunters chafing under having those reckless Crimson River Mercs horn in on THEIR operation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3016-prince-of-ashes","name":"Prince of Ashes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T20:05:48-07:00","id":141185,"title":"","content":"And the compact level of the merit? I have to imagine that the Union doesn't quite have the same level of Night Job as TFV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T23:57:16-07:00","id":141289,"title":"","content":"How does this tie into the Profession Merit? the elephant in the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T19:48:32-07:00","id":142017,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's any significant overlap with the profession merit. Night job only delivers the benefits of belonging to a front organization that your compact/conspiracy runs, while profession is about the capabilities and networking developed by actually doing a job. Someone with an overlapping Night job and profession is someone who could actually do that job, or does so in a capacity directly related to the hunt.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the compact version of the merit, I don't see any need for a mechanical difference between the two. I just imagine compact members having either low ratings or just not having it.<br /> The entire idea of union members paying one of their number to hunt for them is probably an affront to most chapters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3016-prince-of-ashes","name":"Prince of Ashes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:43:53-07:00","id":142427,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd be tempted to make it more of a flat cost thing, 1 or 2 points as a protection from resource degradition from hunting related activities, (possibly with a free skill spec or point of contacts - more in line with professional training.) The flat investigation penalty on finding irregularities doesn't make a huge amount of sense, it cuts off one avenue of investigation but on the other hand the orgainisation itself is a potential irregularity.<br /> <br /> On the compact's front it's worth remembering certain compacts have an absurd amount of economic power as well, the Barrett group or Ashwood Abbey could both support someone on a really good salary quite easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/711-mcgonigle","name":"mcgonigle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}